```text
clerk, and city attorney of any fact, circumstance, or occurrence that has resulted in or may result in
the cancellation or substantive change of any insurance coverage required by this Agreement, and
failure to do so shall be construed to be a breach of this Agreement.
iv.
In addition, CSO shall provide the City with a copy of the insurance policy and/or
policy endorsement listing the City of Cheyenne as an additional insured. The City’s failure to
request or review such policy, endorsement, or certificate shall not affect the City’s rights or CSO’s
obligation hereunder.
v.
Any insurance company providing coverage under this Agreement shall have a
minimum A.M. Best rating of A- (excellent).
6.
Covenant Against Contingent Fees. The CSO warrants that no person, selling agency or
other organization has been employed or retained to solicit or secure this Agreement upon agreement
or understanding for a commission, percentage, brokerage or contingent fee. For breach or violation
of this warrant, the City shall have the right to annul this Agreement without liability or, in its
discretion, to deduct from the compensation, or otherwise recover, the full amount of such
commission, percentage, brokerage or contingent fee.
7.
Political Activity Prohibited. None ofthe funds, materials, property or services contributed
by the City or the CSO shall be used in the performance of this Agreement for any partisan political
activity, or to further the election or defeat of any candidate for public office.
8.
Religious Activity Prohibited.
There shall be no religious worship, instruction or
proselytization as part of or in connection with the performance of this Agreement.
9.
Records and Accounts. The CSO shall maintain fiscal records and accounts in compliance
with Wyoming law as deemed necessary and appropriate by the City to assure proper accounting for
Program funds. These records shall be made available for audit purposes to the City and will be
retained for three years after the expiration of the Agreement. The CSO shall file with the City
Treasurer an audited financial statement as completed each year with a copy to the Cheyenne City
Council.
10.
Reports and Inspection. The CSO shall make financial, program progress, and otherreports
as requested by the City and will arrange for on-site inspections by the City or representatives at the
request of either.
11.
General Provisions.
a.
Amendments.
Any changes, modifications, revisions or amendments to this
Agreement which are mutually agreed upon by the parties to this Agreement must be incorporated
by written instrument, executed and signed by all parties.
